\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Jesus, full of truth and grace,
\par More full of grace than I of sin,
\par Yet once again I seek Thy face;
\par Open Thine arms, and take me in, 
\par And freely my backslidings heal,
\par And love the faithless sinner still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou know'st the way to 
\par bring me back,
\par My fallen spirit to restore:
\par O for Thy truth and mercy's sake,
\par Forgive, and bid me sin no more;
\par The ruins of my soul repair,
\par And make my heart a house of prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The stone to flesh again convert,
\par The veil of sin again remove;
\par Sprinkle Thy blood upon my heart,
\par And melt it by Thy dying love;
\par This rebel heart by love subdue,
\par And make it soft, and make it new.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ah! give me, Lord, the tender heart
\par That trembles at the approach of sin;
\par A godly fear of sin impart,
\par Implant, and root it deep within,
\par That I may dread Thy gracious power,
\par And never dare to offend Thee more.
\par                                          Amen.
\par \f1 
